{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475056-multiple-actions","id":1475056,"title":"Multiple Actions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-20T13:11:28-08:00","id":1475056,"title":"Multiple Actions.","content":"Hello! I have a question regarding multiple actions. Reading the book confuses me on the matter so far, so I'd like to know how it works!<br /> <br /> Say an Arete 5 Mage casts an effect to set someone on fire and within the same turn turns to shoot someone else within the initiative order. <br /> <br /> He has 3 dexterity and 4 firearms, giving him 7 total dies to work with for the shot and 5 dice of Arete to work with for the effect.<br /> <br /> Does he use two seperate pools or use the lowest, since casting magick is an action too I guess? The book doesn't clarify that much on it from what I've gathered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T14:06:36-08:00","id":1475060,"title":"","content":"Which edition are you using?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T14:15:04-08:00","id":1475061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475056-multiple-actions?p=1475060#post1475060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which edition are you using?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 20th anniversary edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T15:22:26-08:00","id":1475062,"title":"","content":"Multiple action take the smallest dice pool, and you have to assign dice to each task. So you have 5 dice to divide between the two actions.<br /> <br /> The major rule with multiple actions and magic, is that you can't cast more than once in a turn (though you can activate a Wonder with its own Arete rating); no splitting for multiple castings, or using Time magic for multiple full actions and multiple casting.<br /> <br /> Considering how small Arete pools are, you can see how trying to cast and take other actions are very rare to try.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T20:29:14-08:00","id":1475080,"title":"","content":"What Heavy Arms said.<br /> The multiple-action rules in 20th anniversary Mage (and only Mage) have gone back to 2nd ed rules, essentially. Which always was a bit baffling to me.<br /> <br /> With the Revised-style rules, and the 20th rules in Vampire and Werewolf, you get quite more flexibility - for example, the 20th Mage rule does not say a word about how to handle automatic actions in a multi-action turn. There is no rule about how they affect that whole dice-pool splitting. Do they not affect it at all? Can you take unlimited auto-actions per turn? Because as it is written right now, you can.<br /> <br /> With the Revised-style rules it's easy - even if they are not rolled, they just add to the total actions, and thus affect the initial dice count (And prevent some weird unlimited-auto thing).<br /> Along the same lines, the revised rules simply subtract dice (and or increase difficulty, depending) evenly for each action - you *still* have the highest chance of success with things you are best at, and you still have the lowest chance with things you are bad at - they all just uniformly become harder to pull off the more actions you take per turn.<br /> <br /> With the 2nd-style rules, it does not matter if you are an absolute *god* at juggling and could do it blindfolded while balancing on a rope, or are just a lousy juggling amateur - if you try to do it at the same time you do something you are worse at, you are equally hosed. And that just makes no sense to me.<br /> <br /> The Revised-style -&gt; 2nd backstep on multi-actions is a big logic and rules regression. (And I still say 20th Dark Ages Vamp has the best one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-20-2022, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T22:49:58-08:00","id":1475083,"title":"","content":"Um... V20 and W20 both use the old splitting rules in their main dice rolling secions, even if there's some C&amp;P spots from Revised that reference the Revised versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T00:36:43-08:00","id":1475087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475056-multiple-actions?p=1475083#post1475083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... V20 and W20 both use the old splitting rules in their main dice rolling secions, even if there's some C&amp;P spots from Revised that reference the Revised versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ick, even worse. I'm glad that D:AV went with Revised and even improved it (Aside of fixing some other balancing issues)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T01:21:12-08:00","id":1475091,"title":"","content":"Eh. For Mage at least, it doesn't bug me because magical extra actions aren't great, so it's not really ingrained into Mage that you're going to try more than ~2 actions at a time, which makes combat and similar high detail stuff go faster. It's much worse in VtM and WtA where magical extra actions are a much bigger part of the games so weaker mundane multiple actions means magical extra actions are even more dominant in a fight.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why the 20th books went back to the old splitting dice pools thing for the most part... but it's not the worst darling that got kept instead of fixed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}